//! The `touch-action` [CSS](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS) property sets how an
//! element's region can be manipulated by a touchscreen user (for example, by zooming features built
//! into the browser).
//!
//! Initial: auto. Inherited: no.
//! Percentages: not accepted.
//!
//! Keyword effects:
//! - auto: Enable browser handling of all panning and zooming gestures.
//! - manipulation: Enable panning and pinch zoom gestures, but disable additional non-standard
//! gestures such as double-tap to zoom. Disabling double-tap to zoom removes the need for browsers
//! to delay the generation of click events when the user taps the screen. This is an alias for
//! "pan-x pan-y pinch-zoom" (which, for compatibility, is itself still valid).
//! - none: Disable browser handling of all panning and zooming gestures.
//! - pan-down: Enable single-finger gestures that begin by scrolling in the given direction(s). Once
//! scrolling has started, the direction may still be reversed. Note that scrolling "up" (pan-up)
//! means that the user is dragging their finger downward on the screen surface, and likewise
//! pan-left means the user is dragging their finger to the right. Multiple directions may be
//! combined except when there is a simpler representation (for example, "pan-left pan-right" is
//! invalid since "pan-x" is simpler, but "pan-left pan-down" is valid).
//! - pan-left: Enable single-finger gestures that begin by scrolling in the given direction(s). Once
//! scrolling has started, the direction may still be reversed. Note that scrolling "up" (pan-up)
//! means that the user is dragging their finger downward on the screen surface, and likewise
//! pan-left means the user is dragging their finger to the right. Multiple directions may be
//! combined except when there is a simpler representation (for example, "pan-left pan-right" is
//! invalid since "pan-x" is simpler, but "pan-left pan-down" is valid).
//! - pan-right: Enable single-finger gestures that begin by scrolling in the given direction(s).
//! Once scrolling has started, the direction may still be reversed. Note that scrolling "up"
//! (pan-up) means that the user is dragging their finger downward on the screen surface, and
//! likewise pan-left means the user is dragging their finger to the right. Multiple directions may
//! be combined except when there is a simpler representation (for example, "pan-left pan-right" is
//! invalid since "pan-x" is simpler, but "pan-left pan-down" is valid).
//! - pan-up: Enable single-finger gestures that begin by scrolling in the given direction(s). Once
//! scrolling has started, the direction may still be reversed. Note that scrolling "up" (pan-up)
//! means that the user is dragging their finger downward on the screen surface, and likewise
//! pan-left means the user is dragging their finger to the right. Multiple directions may be
//! combined except when there is a simpler representation (for example, "pan-left pan-right" is
//! invalid since "pan-x" is simpler, but "pan-left pan-down" is valid).
//! - pan-x: Enable single-finger horizontal panning gestures. May be combined with pan-y, pan-up,
//! pan-down and/or pinch-zoom.
//! - pan-y: Enable single-finger vertical panning gestures. May be combined with pan-x, pan-left,
//! pan-right and/or pinch-zoom.
//! - pinch-zoom: Enable multi-finger panning and zooming of the page. This may be combined with any
//! of the pan- values.
//!
//! Grammar: auto | none | [ [ pan-x | pan-left | pan-right ] || [ pan-y | pan-up | pan-down ] ||
//! pinch-zoom ] | manipulation
//!
//! Specification: https://compat.spec.whatwg.org/#propdef-touch-action
//!
//! Author guide: https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS/Reference/Properties/touch-action
//!
//! Purpose and value descriptions adapted from MDN contributors (CC-BY-SA-2.5).
//!
//! Generated from @webref/css 8.7.8. Do not edit.

module std.css.properties.TouchAction.

pub struct Property {
    touch_action: std.css.keywords.Auto | std.css.keywords.None | std.css.keywords.PanX | std.css.keywords.PanLeft | std.css.keywords.PanRight | std.css.keywords.PanY | std.css.keywords.PanUp | std.css.keywords.PanDown | std.css.keywords.PinchZoom | std.css.keywords.Manipulation | std.css.Values.Inherit | std.css.Values.Initial | std.css.Values.Unset | std.css.Values.Revert | std.css.Values.RevertLayer
}.
